{"base_rate":0.21663778162911612,"brier":0.04670086655112651,"bss":0.7248128707964603,"bss_hi":0.796953542239073,"bss_lo":0.6462356033509646,"chart":{"base":[342.9,44.1],"fp":[183.8,352.4],"lead":"62,245.8 272,233.3 482,202.6 692,163.9","note":{"base":"skill 0.72 — higher than 99% of cities","fp":"low end +0pp, high end +2pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.2 °C — better than 52% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 1%; promised 88% → rained 86%"},"rel":"62,463.3 151.2,400.3 615,95.7"},"country":"PT","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve"],"ece":0.017850953206239167,"ess":160.6096242399075,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Lisbon</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Lisbon rain forecast is strongly skilful, and honest except at one point on the scale.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>98%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>1%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 577 days, 2024-04-27 to\n2026-03-25. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 10.2 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.72, ranked 1 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(1&ndash;3) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>320</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>5%</td><td class='num'><b>2%</b></td><td class='num'>81</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>27%</td><td class='num'><b>33%</b></td><td class='num'>57</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>75%</td><td class='num'><b>71%</b></td><td class='num'>55</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>98%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">1 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Lisbon</b> <span class=\"muted\">PT</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Strongly skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">honest except at one point</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.72</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>1&ndash;3\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>577 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Lisbon &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Lisbon\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 76.31185185185186,341.55555555555554 153.26947368421054,241.50877192982458 322.084,70.94545454545454 408.791875,18.0 408.791875,29.375 322.084,150.36363636363637 153.26947368421054,324.5263157894737 76.31185185185186,377.5061728395062 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"303.1438474870017\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"303.1438474870017\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,379.725 76.31185185185186,373.01234567901236 153.26947368421054,260.6666666666667 322.084,123.89090909090908 408.791875,23.6875\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 1% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 320 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"379.725\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 5%&amp;#10;It rained 2% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 81 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"76.31185185185186\" cy=\"373.01234567901236\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 27%&amp;#10;It rained 33% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 57 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"153.26947368421054\" cy=\"260.6666666666667\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 75%&amp;#10;It rained 71% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 55 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"322.084\" cy=\"123.89090909090908\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 98% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 64 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"408.791875\" cy=\"23.6875\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(22%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p class=\"muted\">Not enough days in this city's record to split the year into four and still say anything defensible about each part. The split is sh